{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/190","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/190/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/190/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/190/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/190","id":5911719200,"node_id":"I_kwDOT06kyc8AAAABYF2tIA","number":190,"title":"CRF Talker Advertise declares MaxFrameSize 217, over-reserving class A bandwidth","user":{"login":"Mister-M-alt","id":161579364,"node_id":"U_kgDOCaGBZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161579364?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":6,"created_at":"2026-10-18T16:36:53Z","updated_at":"2026-10-19T03:11:15Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Found by the in-house qualification run of 2026-10-18 on the AX7101 (dev e9cbb676, processor 2cbed0a9).\n\n**Behaviour.** The DUT declares its CRF stream's Talker Advertise with a TSpec MaxFrameSize of 217. Its CRF frames on the wire are much smaller. With the class A interval, this over-reserves about 10.9 Mb/s of class A bandwidth for every CRF stream.\n\n**To check first:**\n- IEEE 802.1Q-2018 35.2.2.8.4: MaxFrameSize is the maximum frame size the talker produces for the stream.\n- Find the CRF MaxFrameSize, or the CRF format parameters it follows from, that the Milan base audio formats specification and Milan v1.2 assign to the DUT's CRF format.\n- Then derive the correct value from the CRF format the DUT sends (timestamps per PDU).\n\n**Done when:**\n- the declared MaxFrameSize equals the specified or derived CRF frame size, with its clause cited;\n- a suite case pins the TSpec value;\n- the processor's suites and the parent's consumer gates pass.\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/190/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/190/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}